    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0559" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg477"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Speed</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,
                            Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 2, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I Have the honor to enclose herewith an
                    extract from despatch No. 13, of September 10, 1865, received from William H.
                    Corwin, esq., the chargé d’affaires of the United States in Mexico, and also
                    translations of the decrees recently issued by the party exercising authority in
                    the city of Mexico, in relation to the immigration and colonization in that
                    country, referred to in that despatch.</p>
                <p>I submit these papers with the view of ascertaining whether, under said decrees,
                    peonage or any other form of slavery can be instituted in Mexico.</p>
                <p>I. will thank you for an opinion at your earliest convenience.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Speed, Attorney General of the United
                            States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
